WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.960
Are you still stuck just knitting squares
and rectangles on your knitting machine?

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:06.600
Let's change that.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.480
Short row shaping, also called
partial knitting, is a game changer.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.320
It lets you add curves,
angles and real shape to your knitting.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.920
Think shoulder slopes, bust darts,
even sock toes and heels.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.040
Have you ever wondered how to knit beyond
just plain old rectangles and squares?

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.320
Let me show you how short rows can open up
a whole new world

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.000
for your knitting machine.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.720
Let's get started.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.240
Hi, I'm Sue.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.800
I'm the voice and the hands
behind the Knit it now videos.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.040
Short row shaping or partial knitting
is exactly what it sounds like.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:49.120
We knit part of a row instead of the full
width on the knitting machine.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.160
We do this by putting some needles
in hold while continuing to knit others.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.800
This creates wedges or angles
in the fabric perfect for shaping

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.000
garments and adding dimension.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.400
It's one of those skills that really
levels up your knitting and helps you go

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:14.080
from flat, square pieces to more tailored,
fitted and artistic designs.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.400
Let's take a quick look at how
this works on the knitting machine.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.800
Instead of knitting all the way across
a row, you'll stop short of the full width

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:29.840
by placing some needles in hold
and then you'll continue knitting.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.640
Each row covers fewer or more stitches,
depending on the shape

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:35.800
that you're creating.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:42.240
Notice that there were more rows knit
on the right side and that side

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.840
is longer than the left.

00:01:44.383 --> 00:01:50.080
The key is to prevent holes or gaps
where the short rows start and stop.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:54.160
You can wrap a needle before moving on.

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:59.120
Sometimes you want to skip
that wrap and embrace the holes.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.240
Making eyelets
Depending on the yarn or the design

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:08.160
that you're trying to knit,
the most important thing is to understand

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:11.400
how to plan your short
row shaping in advance.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.080
So where do we actually use short rows?

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.200
Here are just a few examples.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.240
Shoulder slopes for smooth Shoulder seams.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:27.920
Bust darts to create better fitting
Sweaters no matter what your size.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:35.647
Necklines shaping for round or scoop necks
without stair Steps to make

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.640
easier finishing Curved hems.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.920
A beautiful way to add drape or
design interest to a garments.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.320
Sock, heels and toes.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:52.560
Now this is a classic short row use
and knitting circles.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.840
Yeah, you can knit circles
on your machine with short rows.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.960
Short rows are everywhere once
you start looking for them.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:05.520
Keeping track of your pattern and your
needle counts and wrapping

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.040
are key to success.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.360
Plus practice, practice, practice.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:15.000
Even simple shapes like triangles or
wedges are a great way to practice

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.400
and build your confidence fast.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.480
The Knit it now short row classroom has
lots of examples and a couple of skill

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.320
builders to help you get practice
and build your confidence.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.120
With knitting short rows.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.920
Short row shaping may be a little
intimidating at first,

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.680
but once you get the hang of it,
it opens up a whole new world

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:38.160
of possibilities on your knitting machine.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:43.087
If you want more practice or patterns
that use short rows, be sure to check

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.280
out the resources at Knit It Now.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.960
And if you have any questions or short
row success stories, leave a comment.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.920
I'd love to hear from you.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.440
Thanks for watching and happy knitting.

